==Strategy==
At first glance it appears to be a generic Surge stage, and a remake of Breathtaking Waves, but the enemy composition can quickly become messy due to the inclusion of Prof. Owlbrowley. Most Surge Immune units cannot deal with the owl and most of their usual counters are vulnerable to the Surges, so most of the stage's difficulty revolves around finding ways to take them out under these conditions. Rusher units such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:NX]], and [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]] are recommended to take out the Owlbrowleys quickly before they can cause too much havoc.

Try to maintain space while dealing with each of the major threats to give you enough room to deal with each of the Owlbrowleys. [[Talents|Talented]] [[Matador Cat (Rare Cat)|Bellydance Cat]] can help hold the line due to dodging both the [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] and [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemies the stage heavily features. The two Medu-sans can be dealt with [[Paperboy Cat (Rare Cat)|Paperboy Cat]] who can stack up and shred through each of them. For Wicked Face, try to pierce his Shield while he's alone as both Raynard and Red EnerG can deal with most shield piercers. As usual, [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] is excellent at dealing with both the Surges and Aku enemies. Once both of the Medu-sans and the Wicked Face are defeated, the stage is all but complete as the remaining enemies are poor pushers and the Owlbrowleys are easier to deal to with.

